content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Customer",
      "description": "Person looking to rent or buy an instrument"
    },
    {
      "name": "Instrument",
      "description": "Music item offered for rental or purchase",
      "attributes": [
        "Brand",
        "Model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Brand",
      "description": "Maker of an instrument"
    },
    {
      "name": "Model",
      "description": "Specific version of an instrument"
    },
    {
      "name": "Rental Package",
      "description": "Set of items prepared for an instrument rental",
      "attributes": [
        "Rental Agreement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Rental Agreement",
      "description": "Terms the Customer accepts for renting"
    },
    {
      "name": "Purchase",
      "description": "Customer’s decision to buy an instrument"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sales Associate",
      "description": "Staff member helping customers choose instruments"
    },
    {
      "name": "Repair Technician",
      "description": "Person fixing damaged instruments"
    },
    {
      "name": "Inspection",
      "description": "Initial check of instrument condition"
    },
    {
      "name": "Repair",
      "description": "Work done to restore an instrument"
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory Manager",
      "description": "Person managing stock and incoming instruments"
    },
    {
      "name": "Stock Levels",
      "description": "Current availability of instruments",
      "attributes": [
        "Instrument"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Shipment",
      "description": "Incoming delivery of instruments"
    },
    {
      "name": "Store Catalogue",
      "description": "List of instruments available for sale or rental",
      "attributes": [
        "Instrument"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Quality Specialist",
      "description": "Person checking instruments for quality"
    },
    {
      "name": "Standard Check",
      "description": "Quality test for instruments before display"
    },
    {
      "name": "Repair Confirmation",
      "description": "Final approval that a Repair is complete"
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Sales": {
      "objects": [
        "Customer",
        "Sales Associate",
        "Instrument",
        "Brand",
        "Model",
        "Rental Package",
        "Rental Agreement",
        "Purchase"
      ]
    },
    "Quality Assurance": {
      "objects": [
        "Repair Technician",
        "Quality Specialist",
        "Inspection",
        "Repair",
        "Repair Confirmation",
        "Instrument"
      ]
    },
    "Inventory Keeping": {
      "objects": [
        "Inventory Manager",
        "Stock Levels",
        "Instrument",
        "Store Catalogue",
        "Shipment"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Sales": {
      "derived from": "Sales Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Customer",
        "Sales Associate",
        "Instrument",
        "Brand",
        "Model",
        "Rental Package",
        "Rental Agreement",
        "Purchase"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Quality Assurance": {
      "derived from": "Quality Assurance Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Repair Technician",
        "Quality Specialist",
        "Inspection",
        "Repair",
        "Repair Confirmation",
        "Asset"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Instrument -> Asset"
      ]
    },
    "Inventory Keeping": {
      "derived from": "Inventory Keeping Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Inventory Manager",
        "Stock Levels",
        "Instrument Record",
        "Store Catalogue",
        "Shipment"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Instrument -> Instrument Record"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
